namespace pdg { /**
\struct pdg::SpriteBreakEvent
\brief A body exceeded its angular-speed threshold or a legacy joint exceeded its break force.

Register an IEventHandler for eventType_SpriteBreak on the owning Sprite. Part
body notifications use their owning Sprite's route. Inspect reason to distinguish
the two event forms. Body notifications work with both basic and Chipmunk solvers.

\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly
\anchor sprite_break_event_fields
\par Break event fields

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| emitter, eventType | Standard event emitter and eventType_SpriteBreak. |
| actingSprite, inLayer | Owning Sprite and its layer (null outside a layer). |
| reason | physicsBreak_AngularSpeed or physicsBreak_Force. |
| action | action_BodyBreak for speed; action_JointBreak for legacy force breaks. |
| body, part | Source PhysicsBody and optional Part for speed; null for legacy force breaks. |
| referenceBody | Optional angular-speed reference PhysicsBody, otherwise null. |
| angularSpeed | Measured speed magnitude in radians/second; zero for force breaks. |
| breakAngularSpeed | Configured speed threshold in radians/second; zero for force breaks. |
| targetSprite, joint | Legacy joint endpoint and CpConstraint; null for speed events. |
| impulse, force, breakForce | Legacy joint impulse, solved force and break threshold; zero for speed events. |

\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly

Angular-speed notifications do not clamp speed, apply braking, disconnect joints
or split artwork, regardless of the handler's return value. They fire once per
sampled excursion above the limit; returning to or below the limit rearms them.
See PhysicsBody.setBreakAngularSpeed() for sampling and reference lifetime rules.

Legacy Chipmunk joint-force events retain their existing behavior: returning true
handles the notification; an unhandled event invokes the existing disconnect path.
Shared PhysicsConstraint force breaking retains its existing behavior too; this
body feature does not add force events to that separate constraint path.

\see PhysicsBody.setBreakAngularSpeed(), pdg.eventType_SpriteBreak
\ingroup Events
\ingroup Physics
*/ }
